WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:08.202
Hi! Today we'll learn about the angles in a triangle, and some special kinds of triangles.

2
00:00:08.352 --> 00:00:12.450
Cut out a paper triangle and tear off its three corners.

3
00:00:12.600 --> 00:00:17.874
Put the three corners together. They fit exactly along a straight line.

4
00:00:18.024 --> 00:00:27.762
A straight line is 180 degrees. So the three angles of any triangle always add up to 180 degrees.

5
00:00:27.912 --> 00:00:34.506
A triangle has two angles of 50 degrees and 70 degrees. What is the third angle?

6
00:00:34.656 --> 00:00:40.746
180 minus 50 minus 70 is 60 degrees.

7
00:00:40.896 --> 00:00:48.018
An isosceles triangle has two equal sides. The two angles opposite those sides are also equal.

8
00:00:48.168 --> 00:00:54.090
An equilateral triangle has three equal sides, and every angle is 60 degrees.

9
00:00:54.240 --> 00:00:59.874
A right-angled triangle has one angle of 90 degrees.

10
00:01:00.024 --> 00:01:08.202
Let's try one. An isosceles triangle has a top angle of 40 degrees. What is each of the other two angles?

11
00:01:08.352 --> 00:01:16.098
First, 180 minus 40 is 140 degrees. That's the two equal angles together.

12
00:01:16.248 --> 00:01:23.658
The two angles are equal, so 140 divided by 2 is 70 degrees each.

13
00:01:23.808 --> 00:01:30.954
One more: in a right-angled triangle, one angle is 35 degrees. What is the other small angle?

14
00:01:31.104 --> 00:01:38.274
The right angle is 90 degrees, so we work out 180 minus 90 minus 35,

15
00:01:38.424 --> 00:01:42.402
which is 55 degrees.

16
00:01:42.552 --> 00:01:53.154
Watch out! If the question says a base angle is 40 degrees, some pupils still do 180 minus 40, divided by 2. That is wrong!

17
00:01:53.304 --> 00:02:02.202
Both base angles are 40 degrees, so the top angle is 180 minus 40 minus 40, which is 100 degrees.

18
00:02:02.352 --> 00:02:09.666
First check which two angles are equal. They are the ones opposite the two equal sides.

19
00:02:09.816 --> 00:02:21.810
Your turn! An isosceles triangle has a base angle of 65 degrees. What is the top angle? Pause and think.

20
00:02:21.960 --> 00:02:33.354
Both base angles are 65 degrees. 180 minus 65 minus 65 is 50 degrees. Did you get it right?

21
00:02:33.504 --> 00:02:46.002
Another one! A triangle has angles of 48 degrees and 67 degrees. What is the third angle? Pause and think.

22
00:02:46.152 --> 00:02:54.762
180 minus 48 minus 67 is 65 degrees. Did you get it right?

23
00:02:54.912 --> 00:03:07.242
Remember: the three angles in a triangle add up to 180 degrees. An isosceles triangle has two equal angles, and an equilateral triangle has three 60 degree angles.

24
00:03:07.392 --> 00:03:11.586
Now go and practise in your garden!

